Hi,

can any HDSP owner with 2.6 kernel test the attached patches?

The patch changes the firmware loading of hdsp.  When the hotplug
firmware loader on kernel is available, it uses automatically via
hotplug.  So, hdsploader is no longer needed.

The patches are for alsa-kernel, alsa-driver and alsa-firmware,
respectively.  After applying them, rebuild alsa-driver, and reinstall
alsa-firmware, too.

Please let me know if it works, then I'll commit these patches to CVS
before 1.0.8-rc2.


thanks,

Takashi

--Multipart_Wed_Dec_29_14:28:04_2004-1
